mike/kb/archive/2026-W26-W27-raw-events.md:1936:- [[REDACTED]28T05:35:50Z] Taylor/finding — pipeline-data-quality-review: {"issues": [{"id": "DQ-1", "severity": "HIGH", "component": "[D] process_stock_indicator daily_update=True -> app dataset tail(10)", "description": "On daily runs only merged.tail(10) is written into ticker_v1a and only the current-month v1/indicator partition is updated. A corporate action (split/stock dividend/oshares change) re-adjusts the ENTIRE VCI adjusted-price history, but only the last 10 rows of ticker_v1a get the new adjusted values. Older rows keep pre-adjustment Close -> a price discontinuity/jump at the 10-row seam.", "impact": "Every adjusted-price-derived indicator that spans the seam is corrupted: MA10/20/50/200, RSI, MACD (long EMA memory), CMF, CMB, VAP1W/1M/3M, Sup/Res_1Y, Close_T1W, C_L1W/C_L1M, volume_Max1Y/5Y, T1W/T2W/T1M/T3M ratios, and all profit_* targets. MAs/long-window stay wrong for their full lookback. Poisons BOTH ML training rows and the live signal row. The doc shows the oshares-change path calls process_stock_indicator but does NOT state daily_update=False, so the corp action is likely never fully back[REDACTED] in daily ops.", "fix": "On ANY corp action / oshares change, force a full-history recompute (daily_update=False, upload=True) for that ticker so the entire adjusted series + monthly partitions + BQ are rebuilt, not just tail(10). Add a guard that detects an adjusted-Close ratio jump vs prior cache and auto-escalates to full rebuild."}, {"id": "DQ-2", "severity": "HIGH", "component": "[D] app-facing dataset step: 'fill last row NaN tu row truoc'", "description": "The app-dataset build forward-fills the last row's NaNs from the previous row across columns. The newest row legitimately has NaN forward-looking targets (profit_2W/1M/2M/3M need future bars) and possibly not-yet-released fundamentals. Forward-filling fabricates non-null values for exactly the most recent row -> the row live screening (universe_scan / score_live_signals) consumes.", "impact": "Look-ahead contamination on the live signal row: profit_* (forward-looking, KB rule: NEVER a live filter) get [REDACTED] with the prior day's realized value, and stale fundamentals get carried. If any live filter or scoring touches a forward column it silently leaks future information. Also injects fabricated targets into BQ ticker via [H].", "fix": "Restrict the last-row NaN-fill to a whitelist of point-in-time-safe columns only (e.g. carry-forward fundamentals that are genuinely sticky). NEVER fill profit_* / any forward-looking column. Assert profit_* are NULL for the most recent ~60 trading days before BQ append."}, {"id": "DQ-3", "severity": "MED", "component": "[A2] update_stock_price / load_full_unadjust_price_history (cafef ~20 phien)", "description": "Unadjusted price merge = full local cache + latest ~20 sessions from cafef, dedup keep-last. If the pipeline misses >20 trading days, the gap between cache-end and the latest-20 window is never fetched -> a hole in the unadjusted Price series (dedup cannot fill missing middle dates).", "impact": "merge_adjust_unadjust reconciles Price off the unadjusted feed; a gap produces NaN/ffill [REDACTED] in unadjusted Price -> wrong Trading_Value (Price x Volume), VAP, and any unadjusted-Price filter for the gap window. Adjusted indicators survive (VCI is full-history). Tet (~9d) is safe; a multi-week outage / DR is not.", "fix": "On startup compare cache max(time) to today; if gap > ~15 trading days, escalate to a backfill path (read all GCS rawdata/price partitions, or daily_update=False) instead of trusting the 20-session window. Add a freshness assert before preprocess."}, {"id": "DQ-4", "severity": "MED", "component": "[A2] update_stock_adjust_price delete-before-upload (non-atomic)", "description": "Daily path deletes preprocess/adjusted_price/{ticker}.csv to reset blob.updated, THEN uploads rawdata + re-writes preprocess. If the process dies / VCI fails between delete and the preprocess write, the file is gone.", "impact": "[D] compute_indicators reads preprocess/adjusted_price/{ticker}.csv as INPUT -> that ticker fails and is skipped for the day (dropped from app dataset + BQ sync). is_monitor for it goes false (no fresh blob) -> ticker silently drops from the monitored/screening universe. Self-heals next full run, but a persistent VCI failure = ongoing data loss for that name. This is a real anti-pattern: coupling a metadata-timestamp hack to data integrity.", "fix": "Don't delete to bump a timestamp. Either (a) upload to a temp blob then atomic copy/rename over the target, or (b) set custom blob metadata for the monitor flag, or (c) compute is_monitor from data content (max(time) in file == today) instead of blob.updated."}, {"id": "DQ-5", "severity": "MED-HIGH", "component": "[H] sync_bigquery_table_batch financial latest_rows_per_ticker=1", "description": "Financial BQ sync writes only the single newest quarter row per ticker (window-7/5-rows applies to price tables, not financial). Revisions to PRIOR quarters (preliminary -> audited Q4, restatements, NP/Revenue corrections) are not re-synced once a newer quarter becomes 'latest'.", "impact": "tav2_bq.ticker_financial keeps stale preliminary values for already-superseded quarters -> backtests over those quarters train/eval on numbers the company later revised. Also if the pipeline misses the window during a quarter transition, that quarter's final value can be stranded. Missing 1 day on price tables is fine (5-row overlap self-heals); financial is the weak link.", "fix": "For financial sync, detect revised quarters (compare hash/Release_Date vs BQ) and re-upsert the affected historical quarter rows, not just the latest. Or periodically run replace_ticker_data_in_bigquery_table for the financial table over the last ~8 quarters."}, {"id": "DQ-6", "severity": "MED-HIGH", "component": "[G] update_market_regime_state DT5G BQ sync (tail 5) + get_gated_state freshness", "description": "DT5G writes vnindex_5state_dt5g_live with only the last 5 trading days. Missing >5 trading days leaves an actual gap (missing dates) in the state table, not just a stale last row. The DT5G base uses ffill (known ffill-frozen bug, [REDACTED]02) which masks staleness as a flat repeated state. get_gated_state() fails-closed on macro_health.json feed freshness (VIX/SPX/SBV) but does NOT check the freshness/continuity of the dt5g_live table itself.", "impact": "A stale or frozen state silently disables the risk gate -> sizing (V2.4 allocator w_LAG by state, go-live [REDACTED]) uses an old regime; over/under-allocation with no alarm. Date-joining backtest consumers get NULL state for gap days -> mis-default. The gate is insurance; a frozen gate = no insurance, exactly the ffill-frozen failure class.", "fix": "Add a table-freshness/continuity guard inside get_gated_state: if max(time) of dt5g_live is older than N trading days, fail CLOSED to DT4 and fire a Telegram alert. Widen the DT5G sync window (e.g. last 15 rows) to self-heal short misses. Add a watchdog on max(time) drift."}, {"id": "DQ-7", "severity": "MED", "component": "Pipeline vs update_financial_reports — no ordering barrier (timing leak Q1/Q7)", "description": "update_financial_reports runs on beat at 12:00 (intraday/lunch) & 21:00; pipeline() has no beat and no declared dependency on the financial flow — it just reads preprocess/financial_report/*. There is no lock/done-marker. Financial flow sleeps(3)/ticker over hundreds of tickers (long run). If do_report.sh fires while the financial flow is mid-run, compute_indicators reads a mixed snapshot: some tickers updated to the new quarter, some not.", "impact": "On release days the universe gets an inconsistent fundamental snapshot (PE/PB/ROE/FSCORE/PEG mixed old/new across names) -> cross-sectional rating/screening distorted. Separately, the 12:00 intraday financial run can trigger oshares-change -> process_stock_indicator -> BQ write DURING trading hours off a possibly-incomplete same-day price partition (partial-bar contamination).", "fix": "Gate pipeline start on a financial-flow completion marker (lock/sentinel), or schedule do_report.sh strictly after the 21:00 financial run finishes with margin. Make financial preprocess writes atomic (temp+rename) so a half-written ticker file is never read. Avoid intraday indicator/BQ recompute; defer oshares-change rebuilds to the EOD run."}, {"id": "DQ-8", "severity": "MED-HIGH", "component": "Q1 financial point-in-time (Release_Date gating) in compute_fa_indicator_v2", "description": "Financials are stored under quarter={year}Q{n} and joined to ticker by (ticker, time). The doc does not show that fundamentals are gated by Release_Date when building the historical FA series. If a quarter's ratios are applied to dates from quarter-end rather than from actual public release, fundamentals appear in the indicator/BQ series BEFORE the market knew them.", "impact": "Classic look-ahead leak in PE/PB/ROE/FSCORE/PEG/PEG history used by backtests — inflates any fundamentals-conditioned edge. Affects every fundamentals-gated strategy and the 8L rating backtests.", "fix": "Verify compute_fa_indicator_v2 stamps each quarter's fundamentals as visible only from Release_Date/ID_Release (not quarter-end time). If not, re-derive the FA series with Release_Date gating and re-audit affected backtests. This is a verify-before-trust item — flag to confirm against code."}, {"id": "DQ-9", "severity": "MED", "component": "[D] input preprocess/others/risk_indicators.csv (KB: risk_rating dup rows)", "description": "KB known issue: tav2_bq.risk_rating contains duplicate (ticker, quarter) rows. update_risk_indicators (monthly) feeds Beta/Dev into risk_indicators.csv consumed by process_stock_indicator.", "impact": "If dedup (GROUP BY / DISTINCT) is not applied when building risk_indicators.csv, Beta/Dev/Risk_Rating get double-counted or wrongly averaged -> Risk_Rating composite and any beta-gated sizing skewed.", "fix": "Ensure update_risk_indicators dedups by (ticker, quarter) keep-last before writing risk_indicato
